\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Father, if justly still we claim
\par To us and ours the promise made,
\par To us be graciously the same,
\par And crown with living fire our head.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our claim admit, and from above
\par Of holiness the spirit shower,
\par Of wise discernment, humble love,
\par And zeal, and unity, and power.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The spirit of convincing speech,
\par Of power demonstrative, impart,
\par Such as may every conscience reach,
\par And sound the unbelieving heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The Spirit of refining fire,
\par Searching the inmost of the mind,
\par To purge all fierce and foul desire,
\par And kindle life more pure and kind.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The Spirit of faith, in this Thy day,
\par To break the power of cancelled sin,
\par Tread down its strength, o'erturn its sway,
\par And still the conquest more than win.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. The Spirit breathe of inward life,
\par Which in our hearts Thy laws may write;
\par Then grief expires, and pain, and strife:
\par 'Tis nature all, and all delight.\tab 
\par                                      Amen\i .\i0 
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

